# DSH / Mnemon local state
.mnemon/

# AgentTeams run state: the captain/member transcripts are session scratch, and
# they carry absolute paths and machine specifics. Not project knowledge.
.agent-teams/

# One-off review reports from an audit run. Useful while the run is live, stale
# the moment the code moves — the findings that mattered are encoded as checks in
# tools/, so this is the working copy rather than a deliverable.
factcheck-*.md
contract-check-*.md

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Build artifacts.
#
# `data/` is produced by `node tools/build-knowledge.mjs` from `content-src/`
# plus the `VRChat-Agent-Creator-Library` submodule. The only artifact large
# enough to matter is `pages.json` (~3.8 MB), but ALL of `data/` is derived, so
# none of it is tracked.
#
# IMPORTANT — this is not just about repository size: the bundle ships `data/`
# through its `files` whitelist, and the plugin reads it during `apply()`.
# A Harness entry that throws in `apply()` fails STARTUP (dsh-app-boot treats
# every inactive entry as fatal at boot), so an incomplete `data/` would take the
# whole app down. Always run the build before `install_bundle`:
#
#     node tools/build-knowledge.mjs
#
data/

# The preset's plugin rows, derived from the SHIPPED `standard` preset by
# `tools/build-preset-plugins.mjs`. Not tracked because its content depends on the
# DSH version installed: committing one release's row set while calling it "the
# standard agent" would silently pin us to it. `build-knowledge.mjs` regenerates it
# on demand, and fails loudly if it cannot — a short list means a session with no
# file, shell, or skill-loading tools, which looks entirely normal in the GUI.
preset-plugins.json

# Validation/scratch files
.index-check.mjs
